  "text": "An object that can be held on a string and lifted by the wind.\n\nThis flower keeps its own story. Pip stays where you left him.\n\nMara’s earlier story · You guide Mara; Pip stays in the garden\n\nThe tape bridges both torn edges. The wing now holds together.\n\nTrying a gathering plan · Previewing does not send invitations\n\nThe time from one midnight to the next, or its daylight hours.\n\nUnfold or make accessible; an open ending is still unfinished.\n\nPip carries the spare tile. Bring it to Sol beside the ladder.\n\nA girl or woman who has the same parent or parents as someone.\n\nPip takes the remaining repair rope from Grandma’s marked box.\n\n. Move this picture to tell it earlier or later, then release.\n\nSol has the spare tile. Direct him to remove the cracked tile.\n\nThe story writer who welcomes you to SparkFest’s story studio.\n\nGrandma says: “Everyone has agreed. Begin when you are ready.”\n\nYou guide Mara in her earlier story · Pip waits in the garden\n\nFully, exactly, or to some extent, depending on the sentence.\n\nGrandma shared The Empty Bench with the people in the garden.\n\nThe wing is mended. Let the boy carry his bird onto the dock.\n\nGrandma’s friend who repairs things and wrote A Small Repair.\n\nm12 2 2.5 7.5L22 12l-7.5 2.5L12 22l-2.5-7.5L2 12l7.5-2.5L12 2\n\nFeedback stopped. You can ask again for the words shown here.\n\nYour adventure waits while you read, explore or take a break.\n\nGrandma brought the stored cushions back to the garden bench.\n\nHere, used to means something happened regularly in the past.\n\nRina brings Sol a loaf of bread at his workshop to thank him.\n\nTell Mara the current plan and agree who will read her story.\n\nPip puts his chosen memory in the flower he grew with Grandma\n\nGrandma gives Pip a copy of The Empty Bench to take to Mara.",
